worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_native_lanes.js"
  ceiling 396
  rationale "Browser twins of native precedence rows the worker used to leave to the Rust engine (PR #1188, issue #1175 routing probes): agentic_continuation (the seeded handler-rules.lino rule), meta_explanation (rust/src/solver_handlers/meta_explanation.rs: why / how-you-work / architecture questions read from seed roles), how_it_works (the inline-subject mechanism discovery plan of rust/src/solver_handler_how.rs, offline as native renders it), source_refresh and shell_command_transform (rust/src/retrieval_procedures.rs, rust/src/solver_handlers/shell_command_transform.rs; cue words are `source_refresh` / `shell_command_transform` records of data/seed/code-task-cues.lino) and the response-language demonstration (rust/src/meta_method_answers.rs). Every answer renders a seeded response template from data/seed/multilingual-responses-synthesis.lino or multilingual-responses.lino; growth is the ported handlers, not silent regrowth. Raised to 396 for two recogniser boundaries mirrored from Rust: shellTransformCommandSpan (a plain-word prose lead ending at a colon is not part of the looped command, mirroring command_span) and whyQuestionAddressesAssistant (a fronted why-question claims meta_explanation only when it carries an assistant_self_reference word, mirroring addresses_assistant)."
